  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "thm:absorption-law",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Uniformly over every compact subset of\n\\(\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{loc}}\\times[-\\overline h,\\overline h]\\),\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt m(\\widehat\\beta_F-\\operatorname{ATT}_{NT})}{\\sigma}\n\\xrightarrow{p}x_\\star(\\eta,h)-h\\mu_a\\mu_b.\n\\]\nThe exact phase classification is\n\\[\nx_\\star(\\eta,h)=h\\mu_a\\mu_b\n\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n|h|\\leq h_{\\mathrm{crit}}(\\eta).\n\\]\nIf \\(|h|>h_{\\mathrm{crit}}(\\eta)\\), then the minimizer lies strictly between zero and the ATT coordinate in its signed direction:\n\\[\n0<x_\\star(\\eta,h)<h\\mu_a\\mu_b\n\\quad\\text{when }h\\mu_a\\mu_b>0,\n\\]\nand\n\\[\nh\\mu_a\\mu_b<x_\\star(\\eta,h)<0\n\\quad\\text{when }h\\mu_a\\mu_b<0.\n\\]\nThe set \\(\\mathcal A_{\\mathrm{abs}}\\) is relatively open in\n\\(\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{loc}}\\times[-\\overline h,\\overline h]\\), and\n\\[\n\\mathcal A_{\\mathrm{abs}}\\neq\\varnothing\n\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n\\overline h>\\min_{\\eta\\in\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{loc}}}h_{\\mathrm{crit}}(\\eta).\n\\]\nNo assertion is made for \\(|h|>\\overline h\\).",
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:local-geometry",
      "ass:local-amplitude",
      "ass:a-moments",
      "ass:b-moments",
      "def:local-spike-profile",
      "def:absorption-phase",
      "thm:uniform-profile",
      "thm:global-profile-singleton"
    ],
    "justification": "This is the exact local ATT-absorption phase law, including the critical selection and the necessary-and-sufficient reach condition for nonemptiness.",
    "gap": "The strong-signal endpoint does not identify the bounded rectangular threshold or the selected transition path.",
    "consumer": "Within the abstract exact-oracle sensitivity benchmark, it identifies exactly when treatment-supported heterogeneity remains in the coefficient and when fitted factors absorb part of it.",
    "proof_tex": "The definitions of \\(\\widehat x_F\\), \\(h\\), and \\(\\operatorname{ATT}_{NT}\\) give the exact finite-array identity\n\\[\n \\frac{\\sqrt m(\\widehat\\beta_F-\\operatorname{ATT}_{NT})}{\\sigma}\n =\\widehat x_F-h\\mu_{a,N}\\mu_{b,T}. \\tag{1}\n\\]\nThe uniform-profile theorem gives\n\\(\\widehat x_F-x_\\star(\\eta,h)\\to_p0\\) uniformly on compact subsets of the bounded experiment.  The two moment assumptions give\n\\(\\mu_{a,N}\\mu_{b,T}\\to\\mu_a\\mu_b\\).  Substitution in (1) proves\n\\[\n \\frac{\\sqrt m(\\widehat\\beta_F-\\operatorname{ATT}_{NT})}{\\sigma}\n \\xrightarrow{p}x_\\star(\\eta,h)-h\\mu_a\\mu_b. \\tag{2}\n\\]\n\nIt remains to identify the phase.  At\n\\(x_{\\operatorname{ATT}}=h\\mu_a\\mu_b\\),\n\\[\n B_{\\eta,h}(x_{\\operatorname{ATT}})\n =\\kappa h\n \\begin{pmatrix}\n 0&\\mu_a\\sqrt{v_b}\\\\\n \\sqrt{v_a}\\mu_b&\\sqrt{v_av_b}\n \\end{pmatrix}. \\tag{3}\n\\]\nRow and column sign changes are orthogonal transformations.  Thus, with \\(C_\\eta\\) from the absorption-phase definition,\n\\[\n s_1\\{B_{\\eta,h}(x_{\\operatorname{ATT}})\\}\n =\\kappa|h|s_1(C_\\eta). \\tag{4}\n\\]\nOn \\(\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{loc}}\\), \\(\\kappa>0\\), \\(v_a,v_b>0\\), and \\(|\\mu_a|,|\\mu_b|>0\\).  Hence \\(s_1(C_\\eta)>0\\), so every division below is valid.\n\nIn the scalar coordinates of the corrected global-profile singleton theorem, \\(z=0\\) is exactly \\(x=x_{\\operatorname{ATT}}\\), and \\(\\tau(0)\\) is the squared largest singular value in (4).  Its exact selection rule gives \\(z_\\star=0\\) if and only if \\(\\tau(0)^2\\leq c\\).  By (4),\n\\[\n \\tau(0)^2\\leq c\n \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n \\kappa^4h^4s_1(C_\\eta)^4\\leq c\n \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n |h|\\leq\\frac{c^{1/4}}{\\kappa s_1(C_\\eta)}\n =h_{\\mathrm{crit}}(\\eta). \\tag{5}\n\\]\nThis includes \\(h=0\\) and equality at the spectral edge.  The inverse scalar coordinate then proves\n\\[\n x_\\star(\\eta,h)=h\\mu_a\\mu_b\n \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n |h|\\leq h_{\\mathrm{crit}}(\\eta). \\tag{6}\n\\]\n\nIf \\(|h|>h_{\\mathrm{crit}}(\\eta)\\), the same theorem gives \\(0<z_\\star<z_0\\) and\n\\[\n x_\\star(\\eta,h)\n =\\frac{\\operatorname{sgn}(h\\mu_a\\mu_b)}\\kappa(z_0-z_\\star),\n \\qquad\n h\\mu_a\\mu_b\n =\\frac{\\operatorname{sgn}(h\\mu_a\\mu_b)}\\kappa z_0. \\tag{7}\n\\]\nBecause \\(\\kappa>0\\), equation (7) gives\n\\[\n 0<x_\\star(\\eta,h)<h\\mu_a\\mu_b\n \\quad\\text{if }h\\mu_a\\mu_b>0,\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n h\\mu_a\\mu_b<x_\\star(\\eta,h)<0\n \\quad\\text{if }h\\mu_a\\mu_b<0. \\tag{8}\n\\]\n\nThe entries of \\(C_\\eta\\), its largest singular value, \\(c^{1/4}\\), and \\(\\kappa\\) are continuous on \\(\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{loc}}\\).  The denominator in (5) is positive and, by compactness, bounded away from zero.  Thus \\(h_{\\mathrm{crit}}\\) is continuous and positive.  The strict inverse image\n\\[\n \\mathcal A_{\\mathrm{abs}}\n =\\{(\\eta,h):|h|>h_{\\mathrm{crit}}(\\eta)\\}\n \\cap\\{(\\eta,h):\\eta\\in\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{loc}},\\ |h|\\leq\\overline h\\}\n\\]\nis relatively open.  Compactness of \\(\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{loc}}\\) implies that \\(h_{\\mathrm{crit}}\\) attains its minimum.  If \\(\\mathcal A_{\\mathrm{abs}}\\neq\\varnothing\\), its defining inequality implies\n\\[\n \\overline h>\\min_{\\eta\\in\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{loc}}}h_{\\mathrm{crit}}(\\eta). \\tag{9}\n\\]\nConversely, if (9) holds, choose a minimizer \\(\\eta_0\\) and any \\(|h|\\in(h_{\\mathrm{crit}}(\\eta_0),\\overline h]\\); then \\((\\eta_0,h)\\in\\mathcal A_{\\mathrm{abs}}\\).  This proves the exact nonemptiness equivalence without an additional reach assumption.  All stochastic uses above invoke \\(|h|\\leq\\overline h\\), so no conclusion has been extended beyond the bounded experiment.",
